@SeasonId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@PhaseId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Rounds of a season, in the season order (take the ids from GET /seasons; defaults: offset 0, limit 25)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/rounds?seasonId={{SeasonId}}
Accept: application/json

### Page through the rounds
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/rounds?seasonId={{SeasonId}}&offset=0&limit=10
Accept: application/json

### Only the rounds of one phase (take the id from GET /seasons/{id})
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/rounds?seasonId={{SeasonId}}&phaseId={{PhaseId}}
Accept: application/json

### Unknown season: 200 with empty items
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/rounds?seasonId=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Accept: application/json

### Error: seasonId is required (400)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/rounds
Accept: application/json

### Error: seasonId is not a GUID (400)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/rounds?seasonId=not-a-guid
Accept: application/json

### Error: limit above the maximum of 100 (400, errors.limit)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/rounds?seasonId={{SeasonId}}&limit=1000
Accept: application/json

### Error: negative offset (400, errors.offset)
GET {{DataApi_HostAddress}}/api/{{ApiVersion}}/rounds?seasonId={{SeasonId}}&offset=-1
Accept: application/json
